\fB\&-nodepchk\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Ignores unknown potential data dependencies. This is especially useful in \
disambiguating unknown data dependencies arising from use of array \
subscripts that cannot be derived at compile-time. For example, if an array is \
referenced in a loop using the induction variable plus some other \
non-induction-based variable as a subscript, the compiler must assume that \
the array conflicts with a similar array reference based on the induction \
variable alone. If it is known that the two array references do not conflict, then \
this switch may result in better code. Do not use this switch if such data \
dependencies do exist. 
.RE
